urem-s: x % y, for x from 0 to 999 and y from 1 to 999.
Cells 88-98. To call it, put y in cell 96, load x into the accumulator and JMP 88.
It returns x % y in the accumulator.
It overwrites its own cells and cell 99; y in cell 96 is kept.
Size 11 cells. It runs at most 3,005 instructions, 17.9 on average, counted from cell 88 to the return jump in cell 98.
Exact over the domain.

cell  contents   notes
 88     695      STO 95   cells 88-90: the call: store x, and copy the return jump from cell 99 into cell 98
 89     199      CLA 99
 90     698      STO 98
 91     195      CLA 95   cells 91-94: take y away until the accumulator goes below 0
 92     796      SUB 96
 93     397      TAC 97
 94     892      JMP 92
 95     000      data: x
 96     000      data: y, which is kept
 97     296      ADD 96   cell 97: that went one y too far: add it back
 98     000               set on every call: the jump back to the caller
